From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 13:45:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: tag_mxl862xx_8021q: stamp skb queue_mapping with port index

MediaTek QDMA's ndo_select_queue derives the PPPQ qid from
skb->queue_mapping. Generic 8021Q taggers leave it untouched, so every
MXL862 user-port flow lands on the conduit base queue and per-port rate
caps have no effect. Set queue_mapping = dp->index in
mxl862_8021q_xmit() before dsa_8021q_xmit().

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 net/dsa/tag_mxl862xx_8021q.c |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/net/dsa/tag_mxl862xx_8021q.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_mxl862xx_8021q.c
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ static struct sk_buff *mxl862_8021q_xmit
 	u16 tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_standalone_vid(dp);
 	u16 queue_mapping = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb);
 	u8 pcp = netdev_txq_to_tc(netdev, queue_mapping);
+	skb_set_queue_mapping(skb, dp->index);
 
 	return dsa_8021q_xmit(skb, netdev, ETH_P_8021Q,
 			      (pcp << VLAN_PRIO_SHIFT) | tx_vid);
